== Homework B2 | ECON 0100 | Fall 2026

_Due: Sunday, Sep. 20_

Homework is designed to both test your knowledge and challenge you to apply familiar concepts in new applications. Answer clearly and completely, and show your work so you can later understand your thought process. You are welcomed and encouraged to work in groups as long as your work is your own. Submit your answers on Gradescope when you're finished: each answer there is a selection.

=== Butterbeer

The supply curve for butter beer can be represented by the following equation:

$ P = 20 + 1/2 Q $

Prices are in galleons and quantity is in bottles.

=== Q1 | Quantity Supplied

Use a graph to plot this supply curve, including the quantity supplied at both $40$ galleons and $50$ galleons.

a) Quantity supplied at $40$ galleons:#blank

b) Quantity supplied at $50$ galleons:#blank

c) How much did quantity supplied change as the price dropped from $50$ to $40$?#blank

d) What is marginal cost at a quantity of $60$?#blank

